{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/332104-wyrd-evolution-for-the-mechanical-seeming","id":332104,"title":"Wyrd Evolution for the Mechanical Seeming.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-06T03:59:21-08:00","id":332104,"title":"Wyrd Evolution for the Mechanical Seeming.","content":"Blessings:<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 7, Skill Specialties now grant a +4 bonus. All non Contract rolls involving Crafts gain the 8 Again bonus. This includes making Tokens and Hedgespun.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 8, you may spend glamour to improve dice pools involving any man made device on a 1:2 basis. The number of turns you may spend glamour this way per day is limited to your current Willpower + Wyrd/2 round up. You cannot spend glamour to repair or build man made devices, only to use them.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 9, you may use the Wyrd 8 blessing as often as you have glamour left. Also, your technological affinity allows you to further repair or syphon technology with a mere touch. As an instant action, you convert 1 point of Structure into 1 point of glamour or vice versa, bypassing the Durability. You may do this once per scene, and any glamour not spent by the end of the scene vanishes. The maximum number of Structure/glamour points that can be repaired/syphoned per day is equal to Wyrd + Willpower and may be divided among multiple devices. Repairs made this way last for the next full day, unless you get an Exceptional Success on a reflexive Wyrd + Crafts/2 round up roll (apply the Wyrd 7 bonus on this roll), in which case the repair lasts indefinitely.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 10, you may heal yourself as if you were a machine. You may spend 1 glamour gained through the previous Wyrd blessing to heal 1 lethal damage or 2 bashing damage. Aggravated damage may NOT be healed this way. You may still benefit from normal medical help. The amount of glamour points you can spend this way per chapter (game session) is equal to Stamina + Crafts.<br /> <br /> Curses:<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 7, the ADDITIONAL penalty for Untrained Skills is -3 instead of -2.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 8, you do not gain the 10 Again bonus on mundane Wits rolls, and any 1s that come up take away a success.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 9, any extended Wits roll is capped by your current willpower rating. This does not apply to making Hedgespun.<br /> <br /> At Wyrd 10, spending willpower on all Wits and Untrained Skill rolls only grants a +1 bonus. Also, unless you are using a Skill Specialty, you lose the 10 again bonus. The exception to this is Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-10-2014, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T12:09:50-08:00","id":336197,"title":"","content":"Where's the Mechanical Seeming from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value